From 3370a372c96635dc2888dcc38804799c4c2dcbea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikhil Idiculla <nikhil.idiculla@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:27:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Keep short Unicode Strings in one native WasmGC array

---
 TOUR.md                                     |  19 +-
 src/snail-scheme/strict-wasm.sld            | 254 ++++++++++++--------
 tests/strict/cases.json                     |   5 +
 tests/strict/string-hybrid-range-errors.scm |  25 ++
 tests/strict/string-hybrid.scm              |  60 +++++
 5 files changed, 252 insertions(+), 111 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/strict/string-hybrid-range-errors.scm
 create mode 100644 tests/strict/string-hybrid.scm

diff --git a/TOUR.md b/TOUR.md
index 2f3e4ec..a01c973 100644
--- a/TOUR.md
+++ b/TOUR.md
@@ -270,14 +270,17 @@ procedure inside its lexical scope. This also keeps named-let recursion direct
 without changing the expanded or checked frontend forms.
 Invariant vectors use native
 array element storage; I64 index checks precede narrowing, while native array
-instructions own bounds and overlapping-copy behavior. Each String has an
-immutable owner containing writability, unsigned scalar length, a direct first
-character block and an optional directory of remaining blocks. Its private i32
-arrays each hold at most 8,192 Unicode scalars; short and empty strings omit the
-directory. Constructors publish only fully initialized, independently owned
-blocks. Copies validate both complete I64 ranges before traversing bounded native
-array-copy spans in the overlap-safe direction. Readonly literal globals and
-fresh mutable strings share the same layout.
+instructions own bounds and overlapping-copy behavior. A short String is one
+private i32 array containing permission followed by at most 8,192 Unicode
+scalars. A longer String has an immutable owner containing permission, unsigned
+scalar length, a full first character block and a directory of remaining
+blocks. A private nonnullable WasmGC eq reference carries these two storage
+forms; concrete source typing and Top's semantic witness still identify String.
+Constructors publish only fully initialized, independently owned payloads,
+including fresh empty arrays. Copies validate both complete I64 ranges before
+writing. Two flat arrays use one native array.copy; other copies traverse bounded
+spans in the overlap-safe direction. Readonly literals choose the same storage
+forms by length.
 Unicode scalar conversions reject surrogate and out-of-range values. Nominal records use immutable native fields;
 closed sums add a constructor tag and typed case subtypes. The layout registry
 reserves applications before following recursive fields, and accessors explicitly
